      "writtenOn": "2026-10-20T13:31:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "compared to the other test cases naming pattern `\u003csubject\u003e_\u003coutcome\u003e` this one misses the `_\u003coutcome\u003e` part.\n\nIn general, I would suggest to rather start from simple building blocks like reading one expression key and asserting that it works both as single and multi-expression. When such a test passes then it implies that reading each key is proper and we don\u0027t need to code many test variants for different combinations (where we can never cover all possible combinations).",
